# Generated PDFs are binary release/site artifacts. Do not text-diff or normalize them.
*.pdf binary

# Committed evidence whose bytes are hash-anchored. `bundle.json` records the
# SHA-256 of every file beside it and `habitable verify` re-derives them, so any
# line-ending normalisation on the way into (or out of) the object store makes a
# fixture fail in a fresh clone while passing on the machine that wrote it.
#
# This is not hypothetical: `git add` of an RFC 5322 message under
# `core.autocrlf=input` staged a blob with ZERO carriage returns where the file
# on disk had 29 (issue #304). CRLF is mandatory in a mail header block, so the
# committed packet would have verified locally and failed in CI on a byte no
# renderer touched. The warning `git add` prints scrolls past in a wall of `A `
# lines.
#
# Check by comparing the STAGED BLOB to the worktree file, never `git hash-object`
# against your intention -- that applies the same filter and agrees with itself:
#     git cat-file -p "$(git ls-files -s <path> | awk '{print $2}')" | tr -dc '\r' | wc -c
/tests/golden/** -text
/site/sample-packet/** -text
